{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l2km8okm","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"physics","chapter":"current-electricity","chapterGroup":"electricity","topic":"meter-bridge","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pa-meter-bridge-is-set-up-as-shown-to-determine-an-unknow-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-gi1d3powx9rad3vw","content":"<p>A meter bridge is set up as shown, to determine an unknown resistance X using a standard 10 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.633ex\" height=\"1.593ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 722 704\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"3A9\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3A9\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> resistor. The galvanometer shows null point when tapping-key is at 52 cm mark. The end-corrections are 1 cm and 2 cm, respectively, for the ends A and B. The determined value of X is</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2lx84nb/d545d9dc-251f-4391-a904-5d41578e6d2d/71adb970-c88c-11ec-9050-c7c5cf4de110/file-1l2lx84nc.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l2lx84nb/d545d9dc-251f-4391-a904-5d41578e6d2d/71adb970-c88c-11ec-9050-c7c5cf4de110/file-1l2lx84nc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Current Electricity Question 19 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l2lx84nb/d545d9dc-251f-4391-a904-5d41578e6d2d/71adb970-c88c-11ec-9050-c7c5cf4de110/file-1l2lx84nc.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l2lx84nb/d545d9dc-251f-4391-a904-5d41578e6